{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1382364-homebrew-the-coil-of-erysichthon","id":1382364,"title":"[Homebrew] The Coil of Erysichthon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-18T12:14:53-07:00","id":1382364,"title":"[Homebrew] The Coil of Erysichthon","content":"<i>And dread Hunger embraced [Erysichthon] as he slept, flowing into his throat, his breast, his lips, draining the strength from his hollow veins.</i> - Ovid, Metamorphoses VIII<br /> <br /> All Kindred struggle with their hunger for blood, but Revenants even more so than others. Some have turned to the Ordo Dracul seeking a cure\u2014and while none have entirely succeeded, they have managed to find ways to stave off the worst of it.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Blood Seeps Slowly</b>: By extracting their own vitae before daysleep or torpor, mixing it with certain ingredients, and injecting it back into their veins, the Dragon can preserve it more effectively until they awaken. A revenant waking from daysleep, or a vampire waking from torpor, retains vitae equal to their Blood Potency or half what they fell asleep with, whichever is lower. A full vampire waking from daysleep loses only one vitae every [Resolve] days, rather than one per day.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Blood of Beasts</b>: Sometimes blood is scarce and every last drop is precious; scribes of the Hunger need to make the most of what they can get. Animals of size 0 provide one vitae per two creatures consumed. Larger animals provide their usual rating plus their Size in vitae. Kindred of BP 3 or higher divide this amount by two, and Kindred of BP 6 or higher divide it by two again, but can still take sustenance from it.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Predator as Prey</b>: By drawing vitae directly from another vampire, a scholar of Hunger can use it to stabilize and amplify the power of their own blood. When the Dragon consumes vampiric vitae directly, add the &quot;donor's&quot; Blood Potency to the amount of blood preserved through torpor (or through daysleep for revenants), and to the days spent asleep before spending blood. This benefit can only be used once per feeding.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Glutton's Reward</b>: The Dragon can now consume and store more vitae than their Blood Potency should normally allow, increasing their vitae limit by their dots in this Coil. As long as they have more vitae in their system than their usual maximum, they need not specifically prepare every night to get the benefits of Blood Seeps Slowly.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Perspicacious Blood</b>: At this stage, the process of extracting vitae from blood becomes more efficient. For every two points of vitae drawn from a human, you gain three. For every one point of vitae drawn from a supernatural creature, you gain two. In theory, two Dragons with this Coil could feed off each other indefinitely\u2014but this type of &quot;Hungarian marriage&quot; is absolutely forbidden by the Ordo Dracul, after it nearly led to the complete destruction of the Order in multiple domains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T12:16:27-07:00","id":1382367,"title":"","content":"^ This is my attempt at adapting Chary (from Half-Damned) and the Coil of Blood (from 1e) into a new 2e Coil. (I ignore the rule about Revenants not being able to learn Coils because that's dumb.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T13:05:06-07:00","id":1382372,"title":"","content":"This Coil looks dandy. The only part I would change its the &quot;procedure&quot; from the First Tier. This procedure stuff looks more like a Scale developed during the study of the Coil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T14:50:19-07:00","id":1382387,"title":"","content":"I dislike allowing vampires to create an infinite loop even if it\u2019s supposably forbidden. Given that drinking revenants blood comes with fewer risks than normal this seems ripe for abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T16:15:28-07:00","id":1382405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1382364-homebrew-the-coil-of-erysichthon?p=1382387#post1382387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike allowing vampires to create an infinite loop even if it\u2019s supposably forbidden. Given that drinking revenants blood comes with fewer risks than normal this seems ripe for abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair; an alternative is what the MET book did (vitae multiplied with Perspicacious Blood cannot be multiplied again). I just like the story potential of Hungarian Marriages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T18:11:54-07:00","id":1382416,"title":"","content":"I think it does kinda conflict with the flavor text. Efficiently drinking and filtering Vitae is one thing, but it does make it sound like you're creating Vitae from nothing when you do it on a vamp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T18:30:14-07:00","id":1382421,"title":"","content":"How about rolling to retain Vitae that would otherwise be spent? Not reliable but it would allow you to spend less Vitae without creating an exploitable situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T22:01:39-07:00","id":1382441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1382364-homebrew-the-coil-of-erysichthon?p=1382416#post1382416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it does kinda conflict with the flavor text. Efficiently drinking and filtering Vitae is one thing, but it does make it sound like you're creating Vitae from nothing when you do it on a vamp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely fair. How's this instead? <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Perspicacious Blood</b>: At this stage, the process of extracting vitae from blood becomes more efficient. For every two points of vitae drawn from a human or ghoul, you gain three. For every one point of vitae drawn from a living supernatural creature, you gain two. As vampires have no vitae except what they extract from others, feeding from them is unaffected.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:09:15-07:00","id":1382467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1382364-homebrew-the-coil-of-erysichthon?p=1382441#post1382441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Entirely fair. How's this instead? <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Perspicacious Blood</b>: At this stage, the process of extracting vitae from blood becomes more efficient. For every two points of vitae drawn from a human or ghoul, you gain three. For every one point of vitae drawn from a living supernatural creature, you gain two. As vampires have no vitae except what they extract from others, feeding from them is unaffected.</span><br /> </span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That would still allow ghouls to be used to create more Vitae than it would take to heal them giving free blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T03:39:19-07:00","id":1382486,"title":"","content":"You could check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls\">this thread</a> for additional inspiration and discussions on the topic. There's two Coils of the Ascetic, one Coil of Blood and one Coil of Hunger that all revolve around the gaining and/or spending of Vitae, and plenty of discussions about mechanics and themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1382364-homebrew-the-coil-of-erysichthon?p=1382467#post1382467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would still allow ghouls to be used to create more Vitae than it would take to heal them giving free blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the book never states when Vitae is regenerated; only that people only has Vitae equal to their health boxes and that taking a Vitae requires drinking enough blood to deal lethal damage. If you rule that people regain one Vitae each day (which is how the Vitae phylactery Dread Power works) then gaining more Vitae from a ghoul would not lead to an infinite Vitae loop.<br /> Another way to handle Perspacious Blood could be to remove the cap on how much Vitae you could take from a person. That'd allow you to get much more Vitae per feeding, but you'd have to hurt the victim much more to be able to benefit from this advantage. The drawback is too significant to be the last dot of a Coil though, imo.<br /> <br /> I would personally place Glutton's Reward a little earlier. Since it scales with dot rating it's more fun to see it increase when you purchase additional dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T09:42:45-07:00","id":1382542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1382364-homebrew-the-coil-of-erysichthon?p=1382441#post1382441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Entirely fair. How's this instead? <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Perspicacious Blood</b>: At this stage, the process of extracting vitae from blood becomes more efficient. For every two points of vitae drawn from a human or ghoul, you gain three. For every one point of vitae drawn from a living supernatural creature, you gain two. As vampires have no vitae except what they extract from others, feeding from them is unaffected.</span><br /> </span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the &quot;drinking from other supernaturals&quot; should be a fringe benefit rather than the main feature, as it requires both a merit and the assumption that there are other supernatural creatures in the Chronicle. And I also think a capstone feature shouldn't be something that ends up obsolete eventually, because when an Elder eventually becomes unable to drink Human blood they kinda lose the usefulness of this ability. <br /> <br /> I think something like &quot;When you drink from another Vampire, you gain 2-3 additional Vitae. This isn't an excess amount stored in the body, simply the Dragon's ability to refine and conserve the already-processed blood.&quot; <br /> <br /> I would also honestly add in some kind of ability that keeps the Vampire from forcibly having their blood stolen, such as being drunk from, Kindred Dueling, or the Strix. It seems like a natural fit into the theme of this Coil and there's really not anything in it that I've seen at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}